  "limitations": [
    "A permutation null bounds the false-positive rate only under the null it enforces. It is not an orthogonal assay and cannot distinguish a real inter-chromosomal exchange from any process that produces the same window-level marginals (inherited paralogy, assembly artefact, mapping competition).",
    "Null A destroys spatial autocorrelation: the observed contiguity of eligible windows and of a single donor is exactly what it removes, so a count far above the null says the tract is not explained by window-level marginals alone, not that it is a real exchange.",
    "Null B conditions on the observed positions of eligible windows and only tests donor contiguity, so it inherits whatever produced those positions.",
    "Windows absent from the class-winner table (no alignment at all) are treated as absent windows and break runs; their absence is itself non-random and is preserved rather than permuted.",
    "estimated.identity in the class-winner table is the IMPG dice/coverage identity (equals dice.similarity to <=1e-6), not a base-level % identity. A 1% margin in this metric is not a 1% base-level divergence margin.",
    "All permutations are within one parent-child comparison (PAN027 paternal vs PAN011). Permuting which parental haplotype is the transmitted copy is not possible from this input, as documented under permutation_audit."
  ]
}
